 ## Overview
-AnySplat is a feed-forward method that predicts a set of 3D Gaussian primitives directly from uncalibrated input images, bypassing the need for known camera poses or depth priors during inference [S1, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Splatt3R](16423-splatt3r.md) and [ZeroGS](16425-zerogs.md) by explicitly regressing camera poses and depth maps alongside Gaussian parameters, using a differentiable voxelization module to bridge the gap between pixel-wise predictions and a renderable 3D scene representation [S1, unofficial].
+AnySplat is a feed-forward method that predicts a set of 3D Gaussian primitives directly from uncalibrated input images, bypassing the need for known camera poses or depth maps during inference [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard 3D Gaussian Splatting by regressing geometry and appearance jointly via a transformer-based encoder-decoder, and from other feed-forward variants by employing a differentiable voxelization module to handle the transition from pixel-wise predictions to a renderable 3D structure [S1, unofficial].
 
